From 1788d0561e255580814a5c7d3897714958fd3aad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:35:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: allotment, flower and herb patches at six farms
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem
OpenRune has no Farming: the allotment, flower and herb patches at the six
main farms cannot be raked, planted or harvested.

Change
- Catherby, Falador, Ardougne, Morytania (Port Phasmatys), Hosidius and
  Civitas illa Fortis: rake, plant with a seed dibber, harvest with a spade
  (flowers by hand), with the OSRS Wiki's levels, XP, harvest lives,
  chance-to-save constants and limpwurt/woad yields for 8 allotment crops,
  6 flowers and 14 herbs.
- Growth on the farming clock (allotments every 10 minutes, flowers 5, herbs
  20 of UTC time), also while logged out, shifted earlier by a per-player
  offset of 0-31 minutes that is rolled once and kept across logins.
- Each patch's state is the farming_transmit value the patch multilocs show
  (and RuneLite's Time Tracking reads), written to farming_transmit_a-e while
  the player is in that farm's area. Ripe allotments and herbs show their
  highest ripe value and count down by one as each harvest life is used.
- Inspect: "This is an allotment. The soil has not been treated. <state>".
- Wrong patch: "You can only plant potato seeds in an allotment."
- New module content/skills/farming with the server-only dbtable
  farming_crops (56001, rows 60124-60151), server varps 63714-63761 (patch
  state and last growth minute) and 64053 (growth offset), timer
  farming_transmit (435) and ::growpatches.

Tests
FarmingScriptTest (11 integration tests): chance to save, growth up to the
highest ripe value, the ripe value counting down with harvest lives, every
patch loc's multiloc and ripe ops, rake/plant/grow/harvest of an allotment
(ripe value and transmit varbit follow the remaining lives), a full
inventory, planting checks and the wrong-patch message, area transmit, the
growth offset (rolled once in 0-31, kept, ticks crops earlier) and the
Inspect text.

Data sources
- OSRS Wiki: Farming (Mechanics: Growth timing, incl. Mod Ash 30 Mar 2019 and
  16 Nov 2022 on the per-player offset; Variable crop yield), Allotment
  patch(/Seeds), Flower patch(/Seeds), Herb patch(/Seeds), each seed's yield
  calculator, Limpwurt plant, Weeds, Rake, Seed dibber, Grape seed (Changes:
  "You can only plant grape seeds in a vine patch.").
- RuneLite Time Tracking PatchImplementation / FarmingWorld (transmit values,
  ripe ranges, farm areas).
- Did I Compost (RuneLite hub plugin): Inspect "The soil has not been
  treated." and "The allotment/herb patch is now empty." formats.

Caveats
- Not implemented: disease, compost, watering, protection payments, weed
  regrowth, tool leprechaun, digging up a growing crop, the Guide op,
  scarecrows and flower protection of allotments.
- No yield boosts: magic secateurs, Farming/Max cape, Kandarin and Kourend &
  Kebos diary herb boosts, attas plant, Falador diary XP bonus.
- No Huasca or goutweed, no other farms (Farming Guild, Harmony, Trollheim,
  Weiss, Kastori), no amulet of bounty/nature, herb sack or Tangleroot rolls.
- Unsourced (best guess): the planting, tool and inventory-space messages,
  the Inspect state sentences, "The flower patch is now empty.", action
  timings and animations, the 5-tick transmit refresh, and the countdown
  direction of the ripe values (highest when fully grown).

